{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_spectral_derivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_spectral_derivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.not_knot_factor_spectral_derivation_of_free_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.not_knot_factor_spectral_derivation_of_free_data","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/knot_factor_spectral_derivation.lean#L138-L147","doc":"**The formula is refutable at freely-chosen data**, which is why it is\nnamed rather than carried as a `sorry`.\n\nWith no partitions the sum is empty, so `a_𝒦 = 1` reads `1 = 0`.  Recorded\nas a theorem so a later attempt to \"finish\" this file with a `sorry` fails\nagainst a standing counterexample. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knotFactor_eq_one_of_trivial_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knotFactor_eq_one_of_trivial_braid","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/knot_factor_spectral_derivation.lean#L104-L136","doc":"**The unknot consistency check, derived.**\n\nIf the braid and its mirror have the character of the identity on every\nirrep — `χ_λ(β_𝒦) = χ_λ(β_𝒦*) = χ_λ(𝟙)` — then the spectral formula and the\nPlancherel normalisation together force `a_𝒦 = 1`.\n\nEach summand collapses to `w_λ` because `χ_λ(𝟙) ≠ 0`, which is the\nnon-vanishing the old class carried as `chi_one_ne_zero`; the sum is then\nthe normalisation.\n\nThis is why naming the two propositions recovers content rather than only a\nschema: they combine into a theorem about the caller's data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_spectral_derivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_spectral_derivation","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/knot_factor_spectral_derivation.lean#L90-L102","doc":"**Knot-factor spectral formula** ([`prop:knot-factor-spectral-derivation`]):\n\n`a_𝒦 = Σ_λ w_λ · χ_λ(β_𝒦) · χ_λ(β_𝒦*) / χ_λ(𝟙)²`.\n\n**Named, not asserted** — see the module docstring for why neither a\nprojection nor a `sorry` is the honest form here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelNormalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelNormalised","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/knot_factor_spectral_derivation.lean#L80-L88","doc":"**Plancherel normalisation**: the weights sum to `1` (the Wedderburn\ntrace identity).\n\nNamed over caller-supplied data.  Note this says nothing about the weights\nbeing `dim_q²(V_λ) / [n]_q!` — only that they are normalised. ","signatureChunk":0}]}